on. Depression is a chronic and debilitating illness that often starts in childhood or adolescence. It increases risk for future suicide, substance use, and other psychiatric sequelae. Adolescent depressive disorders are more likely to be recurrent into adulthood than childhood onset depression. Suicide is a fatal complication of MDD and surpasses motor vehicle accidents as a cause of death in adolescents. It has high prevalence among high school students with 20% having contemplated suicide and 8% having attempted each year. While the risk of suicide during an MDD episode is high, it can be paradoxically higher during start of treatment as energy and motivation improve with cognitive recovery from depression."}]}
